  "live_records": {
    "q-340458": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340458",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for cosine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta )+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x-5x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x+5x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(-3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(5x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(7x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)+\\frac{1}{14}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(7x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{14}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\frac{7\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}(-1-0)+\\frac{1}{14}(-1-0) \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{21}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
