    "q-340390": {
      "dom_id": "step-q340390",
      "name": "Question 12",
      "problem": "Evaluate the following integral.\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x=$ {{field-1}}",
      "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the sum and difference formulas for sine:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta +\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta -\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\beta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding these equations, we get the following product-to-sum identity:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ) & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡\\alpha \\operatorname{cos}⁡\\beta  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha +\\beta )+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\alpha -\\beta ))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x) & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x+6x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x-6x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(-3x)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting this into the integral gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(6x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(9x)-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(3x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{18}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(9x)+\\frac{1}{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(3x)]}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{9\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0))+\\frac{1}{6}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(0)) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{18}(0-1)+\\frac{1}{6}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
